#### Article 7

7 - (1) Regional Government conducts prevention of acts of violence against women and children as referred to in Article 6 letter a through empowerment and awareness to Families, Parents, and the Community by providing information, guidance and/or counseling.

2. In addition to empowerment and awareness as referred to in paragraph (1), it shall be implemented by:a. providing material on prevention of acts of violence against women and children in both formal and informal education;
b. opening accessibility to obtain education, training, funding, income enhancement and social services in accordance with applicable provisions;
c. opening employment opportunities for women;
d. building community participation and concern towards prevention and protection of women and children from acts of violence;
e. building and providing a complete and easily accessible information system;
f. building networks and cooperation with law enforcement apparatus, government apparatus, educational institutions, and various non-governmental organizations that work and/or care for women and children; andg. opening an integrated service system for the protection of women and children from acts of violence in every sub-district.

#### Article 8

1. Prevention of acts of violence against women and children as referred to in Article 7, shall be implemented by Regional Apparatus that administer governmental affairs in the fields of:a. social affairs;
b. health;
c. education;
d. manpower;
e. population administration and civil registration:f. women's empowerment, protection of women and children; g. cooperatives and Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises; andh. public tranquility, public order, and community protection (2) Prevention of acts of violence by Regional Apparatus as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented in an integrated and continuous manner based on RPJPD and RPJMD.

## Part Three

Legal Protection

#### Article 9

Regional Government conducts legal protection as referred to in Article 6 letter b, including:
a. providing protection in Safe Houses;
b. providing legal information to victims;
c. providing assistance for victims as witnesses from the investigation process until the verdict; and - 8 -d. providing special legal protection for child victims of acts of violence which may be carried out through the appointment of guardianship in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

## Part Four

Recovery

#### Article 10

Regional Government conducts recovery as referred to in article 6 letter c, including:
a. providing physical recovery at health service institutions; b. providing medicolegal services;
c. assisting the repatriation of victims;
d. providing temporary protection in Safe Houses (safe house); e. providing psychosocial recovery and assistance;
f. providing spiritual guidance services; and/org. preparing family, school, work and community environment, as well as economic empowerment.

## Part Five

Coordination

#### Article 11

Regional Government conducts coordination as referred to in Article 6 letter d, including:
a. conducting coordination and cooperation in handling cases of violence with integrated service institutions; and/orb. conducting coordination and cooperation in handling cases of violence with integrated services between Regions.

## Part Six

Community Participation

#### Article 12

Regional Government encourages community participation as referred to in Article 6 letter e, by:
a. fostering community awareness towards cases of acts of violence against women and children;
b. encouraging the community to actively participate in providing information and reporting acts of violence against women and children;
c. fostering local wisdom in handling cases of acts of violence;
d. organizing strengthening of community groups in handling acts of violence against women and children;
e. disseminating information about laws and regulations related to acts of violence against women and children.

# CHAPTER III

## OBLIGATIONS AND RESPONSIBILITIES

## Part One

9 - General

#### Article 13

Obligations and responsibilities in providing protection to women and children from acts of violence are the joint responsibility of:
a. Regional Government; andb. Community.

## Part Two

Regional Government

#### Article 14

1. Obligations and responsibilities of Regional Government as referred to in Article 13 letter a, include:a. establishing, implementing policies, programs, and conducting cooperation activities in the administration of protection of women and children from acts of violence;
b. facilitating the establishment of institutional protection of women and children from acts of violence and providing support for facilities and infrastructure;
c. allocating budget for the administration of protection of women and children from acts of violence according to regional financial capacity;
d. fostering and supervising the administration of protection of women and children from acts of violence;
e. providing protection services for women and children victims of acts of violence;
f. encouraging and increasing community participation; andg. appointing parents and/or substitute family caregivers as a protective measure for children who become victims of acts of violence.
2. In order to carry out obligations and responsibilities as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regent establishes programs and activities for the protection of women and children in the Regional Action Plan as a basis for Regional Apparatus in implementing the protection of women and children from acts of violence.
3. Regional Action Plan as referred to in paragraph (2), constitutes part of RPJMD.
4. Further provisions regarding the Regional Action Plan as referred to in paragraph (2) shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

## Part Three

Community

#### Article 15

1. obligations and responsibilities of the community as referred to in article 13 letter b, shall be organized in the form of community participation.
2. forms of community participation as referred to in paragraph (1), include:a. preventing the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children;
b. providing protection to women and children from acts of violence;

