c. providing information and/or reporting acts of violence against women and children to law enforcement or authorized parties; andd. participating in handling victims of acts of violence.
3. Forms of community participation as referred to in paragraph (2), shall be implemented responsibly in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

#### Article 16

Every person who hears, sees, or knows of the occurrence of violence against women and children is obliged to:
a. prevent and stop the continuation of acts of violence; b. provide protection to victims;
c. provide emergency assistance; and/ord. assist in the process of submitting an application for protection order.

# CHAPTER IV

## FORMS OF VIOLENCE

#### Article 17

Forms of violence against women and children include:
a. physical violence;
b. psychological violence;
c. sexual violence;
d. neglect;
e. maltreatment;
f. exploitation; and/org. other violence.

# CHAPTER V

## RIGHTS OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF ACTS OF VIOLENCE

#### Article 18

Women and children victims of acts of violence receive the following rights: a. right to be respected for their dignity as human beings; b. right to recovery;
c. right to determine their own decisions;
d. right to obtain information;
e. right to confidentiality;
f. right to social rehabilitation;
g. right to complaint handling that is fast, appropriate, comfortable and according to needs;
h. right of victims and their families to obtain facilities in the judicial process;
i. right to assistance; and - 11 -j. right to security and protection.
